+<div class="card-head"><span class="pid">VAP-LAP</span><span class="chip chip-wd">External proposal</span></div>
 <h3>Legal AI Profile</h3>
 <p>VAP-LAP proposes verifiable records for legal AI workflows, including consultation, document drafting, fact checking and human review. The <a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ailex-vap-legal-ai-provenance/05/">individual Internet-Draft -05</a> describes profile v0.6.0, published on 26 October 2026.</p>
 <p><strong>AILEX</strong> is introduced as a product and use-case reference for considering provenance in legal practice. Explore the <a href="https://veritaschain.org/vap/lap/#ailex">AILEX reference</a> and its <a href="https://ailex.co.jp/service/">published service information</a>.</p>
-<p class="note">VAP-LAP is a proposal, not a registered VAP §4.5.2 profile. The product reference does not establish implementation conformance.</p>
+<p class="note">LAP is outside the VAP v1.2 §4.5.2 profile registry; VAP-LAP is the label used by its proposer, not a registered VSO profile designation. Tokachi Kamimura is the representative of both AILEX LLC and VeritasChain Co., Ltd., which operates VSO, and the LAP -05 editor lists AILEX LLC / VSO as the affiliation. AILEX therefore has a commercial interest in this product reference; it is not an example of adoption by an independent third party. This listing does not establish LAP/VAP conformance, certification or an independently validated implementation.</p>
 <p class="more"><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vap/lap/">VAP-LAP overview →</a> · <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vap-spec/blob/main/proposals/legal-ai-profile/README.md">Proposal on GitHub →</a></p>
 </article>
 </section>
